# Git workflow (mandatory)

## Branches

- `main` — production, deployed to Cloudflare Workers (OpenNext) by the user. **Never push directly.**
- `dev` — integration, protected. **Never push directly.**
- **`dee-<NN>-<slug>`** — canonical branch for WAIA work tied to Linear **`DEE-NN`** (see [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and [`docs/waia-governance/BRANCHING-STRATEGY.md`](../../docs/waia-governance/BRANCHING-STRATEGY.md)).
- **`feature/<scope>-<slug>`** — **legacy** naming; avoid for new work unless Architect-approved and noted in the PR.

## Required steps for every change

1. `git checkout dev && git pull origin dev`
2. `git checkout -b dee-<NN>-<slug>`
3. Implement, run `pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test --run && pnpm build` (full chain before PR per [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) + `/test-and-fix`)
4. `git add -A && git commit -m "DEE-NN type(scope): subject"`
5. `git push -u origin dee-<NN>-<slug>`
6. Open PR via `/prepare-pr` (render body from [`.github/pull_request_template.md`](../../.github/pull_request_template.md), run `preflight-pr-governance.sh`, then `gh pr create --base dev --title "..." --body-file .cursor/pr-body-DEE-NN.md` — do **not** use `--fill` alone when a validated body exists)

## Conventional Commits

Use `DEE-NN type(scope): subject` — e.g. `DEE-402 feat(home): add hero section`, `DEE-402 fix(lint): drop unused import`, `DEE-402 chore(ci): bump node to 22`.

## Hard rules

- If you are unsure — STOP and ask before any git operation.
- Never run `git push --force`, `git reset --hard origin/...`, or rewrite history on shared branches.
- Never commit `.env*` files, secrets, or anything matching `*.key`/`*.pem`.
- Never check in `node_modules/`, `.next/`, `playwright-report/`, `test-results/`.
- One feature = one integration batch = one branch = one PR. Multiple work packages may land in one PR when the integration-ready contract holds ([`INTEGRATION-BOUNDARY-POLICY.md`](../../docs/waia-governance/INTEGRATION-BOUNDARY-POLICY.md)). Don't pile unrelated integration batches into the same PR.
